<title>SWITZERLAND: TABLE - Gotthard Bank H1 profit up 36.6 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Gotthard Bank H1 profit up 36.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Gross profit		   106.3	     vs 77.8</p>
<p> Net revenues		   187.3	     vs 157.8</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>  interest activities	 53.8		vs 47.7</p>
<p>  commissions and fees	92.1		vs 75.4</p>
<p>  trading			 35.8		vs 29.6</p>
<p>  other ordinary results    5.6		 vs 5.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Lugano-based Gotthard Bank is owned 55 percent by Japan's Sumitomo Bank Ltd  </p>
<p> Total operating expenses   81.0		vs 80.0</p>
<p> Cash flow			99.2		up 37.5 pct</p>
<p> Total assets under mngmt   24.8 billion    up 20.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Gotthard Bank said within commission income, revenues from stock trading deserved special mention for rising &quot;by more than 35 percent&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom 41-1-258 7340</p>
</text>
